      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe the risk for harassment is much larger towards the common user being recorded or streamed without their consent, rather than the streamer. I know concern about being unknowingly recorded is stopping people from going to places they would like to go otherwise.\nIf you're streaming somewhere where you run the risk of being harassed, maybe you should be streaming from elsewhere... In particular if that harassment is not just kids being edgy, but maybe people that don't want to be recorded (OTOH the proper conduct in this case would be to just leave when you see someone is recording or streaming).\nJust my 2 cents. (And personally, I certainly don't really mind appearing in streams myself, especially if I have prior or situational knowledge of this fact)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
