      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This issue has recently resurfaced in Japan, and some users are even saying, \"If you don't want to be streamed, don't come to public instances in the first place.\" It is impossible to avoid users who are already streaming in advance, and we believe that user streaming status alone cannot provide protection.\n\nFor instance,During streaming status, a logo and copyright notice will be displayed on the screen to prove that the streaming is legitimate.\n\nRegular users have the option to allow or disallow streaming, and those who set their status to disallow streaming should not be visible to users with streaming status (or should be masked or muted).\n\nOf course, I do not believe this will prevent everything.\n\nI hope you will take into account that some users do not want to see more easy streamers.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
